ation Complete ✓\n\n### Changes Made:\n\n**1. Order Model (Order.kt)**\n- Added `OrderStatus` enum with `ACTIVE` and `CANCELLED` states\n- Added `status` field to Order data class with default `ACTIVE`\n\n**2. Error Handling (ApiError.kt)**\n- Added `ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENTS` error code (409)\n- Added `ORDER_CANCELLED` error code (409)\n\n**3. Order Cancellation (OrderController.kt)**\n- Added `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint that:\n  - Returns 404 if order doesn't exist\n  - Returns 200 with unchanged order if already cancelled (idempotent)\n  - Returns 409 if any shipment is CONFIRMED (all-or-nothing)\n  - Moves order to CANCELLED status\n  - Cancels all CREATED shipments of that order\n\n**4. Shipment Repository (ShipmentRepository.kt)**\n- Added `findByOrderId()` to query shipments by order\n- Added `updateStatus()` to modify shipment status\n\n**5. Shipment Validation (ShipmentController.kt)**\n- Validates orders exist and are not CANCELLED before creating shipments\n- Returns 409 if order is CANCELLED\n- Preserves existing behavior for non-existent orders\n\n**6. Comprehensive Tests**\n- 7 new order cancellation tests covering all scenarios\n- 2 new shipment validation tests\n\n### Test Results:\n- **22/22 tests passing** (all existing + new)\n- Build SUCCESS with no warnings\n- Zero new dependencies added\n- Architecture preserved\n\nAll acceptance criteria met: idempotent cancellation, all-or-nothing semantics, proper error handling, and full integration with existing shipment feature.","ttft_ms":3366,"type":"result","duration_ms":170481,"uuid":"f432cc9e-8e86-42a8-8a03-64324bf29bf8","ttft_stream_ms":781,"time_to_request_ms":21,"first_content_frame_ms":1083,"queued_turn_count":0}

